# Spec 0003. Two checks, and the split between them is deliberate.
#
# lint-staged runs ESLint and Prettier over staged files only, so it stays
# fast and only ever touches what you were already committing.
#
# The typecheck is the whole project on purpose. Types are cross-file: a
# changed return type breaks its callers, and those callers are exactly the
# files you did not stage. A staged-only typecheck would pass while the
# project is broken, which reads as a green light and is worse than nothing.
#
# The production build stays out. It is slow enough that a hook running it
# gets bypassed within a week, and `npm run verify` covers it at the moment
# it actually matters.
npx lint-staged
npm run typecheck
